f england near the  english channel lying beneath 400 feet  of water and this is where it will  remain undisturbed in accordance with  international salvage law and a  widespread protocol for military wrecks  when a u.s navy shipwreck is found our  general policy is to leave it  undisturbed it's a war grave it's a  hallowed site  it's pretty incredible given the size  and depth of the ocean that they can  find anything like this but what what  great work i know and that they use that  u-boat commanders that yeah that log was  how they were able to help discover it  so so sensitive that they still  acknowledge that it is  a gravesite right it's a memorial to  them


